---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SampleRecord from '../components/SampleRecord.astro';
import Notify from '../components/Notify.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

// Keep in step with the status block in the Serenata README.
const milestones = [
  { n: 1, name: 'Ingestion and normalisation', detail: 'TED and eForms XML into a documented open dataset', status: 'In progress' },
  { n: 2, name: 'Classifiers', detail: 'One written, falsifiable hypothesis per classifier, with measured error rates', status: 'In progress' },
  { n: 3, name: 'Entity resolution', detail: 'Buyers and suppliers matched against national company registers', status: 'Planned' },
  { n: 4, name: 'Public API', detail: 'Versioned bulk data', status: 'Planned' },
  { n: 5, name: 'Verification interface', detail: 'Every flag next to its hypothesis and its source notice', status: 'Planned' },
  { n: 6, name: 'Documentation and onboarding', detail: 'Architecture docs, contributor guide, packaging', status: 'In progress' },
];
const repoLabel = site.serenataRepo.replace(/^https:\/\//, '');
---
<Base
  title="Serenata Europa"
  description="An open-source pipeline reading EU public procurement notices and flagging anomalies anyone can verify. Successor to Brazil's Serenata de Amor."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label eyebrow">Serenata Europa</p>
      <h1 class="display serenata-title">700,000 procurement notices a year. Nobody is reading them.</h1>
      <div class="column prose intro">
        <p class="lede">
          The EU publishes around 700,000 public procurement notices annually through TED, and
          since late 2024 they arrive in a machine-readable standard called eForms. Dashboards exist
          for analysts. A continuously running, open pipeline that turns those notices into flags an
          ordinary person can verify does not.
        </p>
        <p>I'm building one.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="block">
      <SampleRecord />
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="brazil">
      <h2 id="brazil">What happened in Brazil</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          In 2016, three of us built Operação Serenata de Amor. It was open source, crowdfunded by
          1,296 people, and it read three million parliamentary expense claims looking for the ones
          that didn't add up. Volunteers checked what it found. That verification work led to 629
          formal complaints against sitting congresspeople.
        </p>
        <p>The project is now stewarded by Open Knowledge Brasil.</p>
        <p>
          Serenata Europa is the same method pointed at new territory: a written, falsifiable
          hypothesis behind every classifier, human verification before anything is published, and
          every claim traceable back to the source record. It's an independent project, though —
          not run or endorsed by Open Knowledge Brasil, which carries no responsibility for anything
          published here.
        </p>
      </div>
      <VideoEmbed
        id="751187741"
        hash="dcdf015080"
        title="Estaleiro Liberdade"
        caption="Estaleiro Liberdade"
        duration="2 min 45 s"
      />
      <dl class="facts">
        <div class="field"><dt>Claims read</dt><dd>3 million</dd></div>
        <div class="field"><dt>Backers</dt><dd>1,296</dd></div>
        <div class="field"><dt>Formal complaints</dt><dd>629</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="flag">
      <h2 id="flag">What a flag means</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          A flag is a statistical anomaly matched against a documented risk indicator. Nothing more
          than that. Most flags have innocent explanations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every flag links to the source notice so you can check it yourself. Every classifier's
          hypothesis and its measured error rates are published. Flags concern institutions and
          companies, never private individuals.
        </p>
        <p>
          The code is AGPL-3.0. The original used MIT; this one uses AGPL so that hosted forks stay
          open, which matters for a project whose entire value is that you can check its work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="now">
      <h2 id="now">Where it is now</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="milestones">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Serenata Europa milestones</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Step</th>
              <th scope="col">Milestone</th>
              <th scope="col">Status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {milestones.map((m) => (
              <tr class:list={{ 'is-current': m.status === 'In progress' }}>
                <td class="milestones__n">{m.n}</td>
                <td>
                  <span class="milestones__name">{m.name}</span>
                  <span class="milestones__detail">{m.detail}</span>
                </td>
                <td class="milestones__status">
                  {m.status === 'In progress' && <span class="blaze" aria-hidden="true"></span>}
                  {m.status}
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="column prose after-table">
        <p>
          The ingestion pipeline runs against real TED notices, and a first classifier — flagging a
          lot that drew one bid in a market where single bids are rare — is built and measured. No
          flag has been published yet: verification, entity resolution, and a privacy review come
          before that. The code is public while it's being written.
        </p>
        <p class="repo"><a href={site.serenataRepo}>{repoLabel}</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="follow">
      <h2 id="follow">Follow it</h2>
      <Notify
        list="serenata"
        lead="I'll write here as it gets built, including the parts that don't work. Leave your email and you'll hear when there's something running."
      />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .serenata-title {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .intro {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .block {
    padding-block: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .facts dd {
    font: var(--headline);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .milestones {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .milestones th {
    font: var(--label);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0 var(--space-4) var(--space-2) 0;
  }

  .milestones td {
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-4) var(--space-4) 0;
    border-top: var(--stroke-hair) solid var(--line);
  }

  .milestones tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: var(--stroke-hair) solid var(--line);
  }

  .milestones__n {
    width: 3rem;
    font: var(--title);
  }

  .milestones__name {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .milestones__detail {
    display: block;
    font: var(--small);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .milestones__status {
    white-space: nowrap;
    font: var(--small);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .is-current .milestones__status {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* A trail blaze marks where the project is */
  .blaze {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 12px;
    margin-right: var(--space-2);
    background: var(--ink);
    vertical-align: -1px;
  }

  .after-table {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .repo {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
